Subject: ntdll: WINE_DISABLE_IMAGE_ASLR, to isolate relocation as a variable (temporary)

Skips the server-assigned load address for DYNAMICBASE images, so a DLL lands on
its own preferred base whenever that address is free.

The question it answers: a DLL that checksums its own loaded image fails once it
has been relocated, because relocation rewrites absolute addresses inside .text
and the bytes stop matching what the checksum covered. Crypto++ built as a FIPS
module does this, and SSFIV ships one -- preferred base 0x42900000, which Wine's
ASLR moves into its 0x60000000-0x7c000000 window. The game then prints "In
memory integrity check failed. This may be caused by debug breakpoints or DLL
relocation." and exits(3). Whether that relocation is the cause is worth one
measurement rather than more argument.

This is not a candidate fix, and the comment says so at the switch:

  - Windows relocates DYNAMICBASE images too, and the game runs there. Crypto++
    has a disk-hash fallback precisely for this case, so the real question is
    why that fallback does not save it here.
  - It does not remove relocation in general: SSLEAY32, LIBEAY32 and OpenLDAP in
    this same game all declare preferred base 0x10000000, so two of the three
    are relocated either way.
  - Wine's ASLR window keeps DLLs out of the low address space; letting them
    scatter to preferred bases fragments the 2 GB a 32-bit game has, and a
    resulting allocation failure looks nothing like its cause.

Environment-gated, so an A/B costs a relaunch instead of a rebuild and the
default is untouched. Drops with the other diagnostics.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index b1cdccf68ab..b20020e9bd5 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3618,6 +3618,47 @@ static NTSTATUS map_image_view( struct file_view **view_ret, struct pe_image_inf
  *
  * Map a PE image section into memory.
  */
+/* ---- WINE_DISABLE_IMAGE_ASLR (diagnostic, temporary) ------------------------
+ * Skip the server-assigned load address for DYNAMICBASE images, so a DLL is
+ * mapped at its own preferred base whenever that address happens to be free.
+ *
+ * This exists to isolate one variable, not to be switched on. A DLL that
+ * checksums its own loaded image fails after relocation -- relocation rewrites
+ * absolute addresses inside .text, so the bytes no longer match what the
+ * checksum covered. Crypto++ built as a FIPS module does exactly that, and
+ * SSFIV ships one at preferred base 0x42900000, which Wine's ASLR moves into
+ * its 0x60000000-0x7c000000 window. The question this answers is whether the
+ * relocation is what breaks it.
+ *
+ * It is NOT a candidate fix, for three reasons worth writing down so nobody
+ * reaches for it later:
+ *
+ *   - Windows relocates DYNAMICBASE images too, and the game runs there, so
+ *     "don't relocate" is a way around the symptom rather than the cause.
+ *   - It does not even remove relocation in general. Three of this game's DLLs
+ *     (SSLEAY32, LIBEAY32, OpenLDAP) all declare the same preferred base
+ *     0x10000000; only the first can have it either way.
+ *   - Wine's ASLR window keeps DLLs out of the low address space. Letting them
+ *     scatter to their preferred bases fragments the 2 GB a 32-bit game has to
+ *     work in, and an allocation failure caused that way looks nothing like its
+ *     cause.
+ *
+ * Environment-gated rather than compiled in so an A/B costs a relaunch instead
+ * of a rebuild, and so the default behaviour is untouched.
+ */
+static BOOL image_aslr_disabled(void)
+{
+    static int disabled = -1;
+
+    if (disabled == -1)
+    {
+        const char *e = getenv( "WINE_DISABLE_IMAGE_ASLR" );
+        disabled = e && *e != '0';
+        if (disabled) ERR( "image ASLR disabled by WINE_DISABLE_IMAGE_ASLR\n" );
+    }
+    return disabled;
+}
+
 static NTSTATUS virtual_map_image( HANDLE mapping, void **addr_ptr, SIZE_T *size_ptr, HANDLE shared_file,
                                    ULONG_PTR limit_low, ULONG_PTR limit_high, ULONG alloc_type,
                                    USHORT machine, struct pe_image_info *image_info,
@@ -3643,7 +3684,7 @@ static NTSTATUS virtual_map_image( HANDLE mapping, void **addr_ptr, SIZE_T *size
         return status;
     }
 
-    if (!image_info->map_addr &&
+    if (!image_info->map_addr && !image_aslr_disabled() &&
         (image_info->image_charact & IMAGE_FILE_DLL) &&
         (image_info->image_flags & IMAGE_FLAGS_ImageDynamicallyRelocated))
     {
